# AyahNow — example environment file.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development if needed. Every value below is a
# safe placeholder — none of these are secrets, and this file must NEVER
# contain a real bank account/IBAN, API key, or any other credential.
#
# All variables are EXPO_PUBLIC_* because Expo inlines them into the
# JS bundle at build time — meaning anything placed here is effectively
# public once the app is built. Never put a secret in an EXPO_PUBLIC_*
# variable, in this file or anywhere else in this project.

# --- Corpus build gating (see docs/CORPUS.md) ---
# "development" (default) allows the demo/draft corpus; "production"
# blocks the build unless the corpus is fully validated and publishable.
EXPO_PUBLIC_CORPUS_ENV=development
